# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of platform.
#
# A .sh file checked out with CRLF on Windows and then packaged fails at exec
# with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" — which is a confusing way to learn about
# line endings, especially inside a Lambda whose only symptom is that every
# invocation dies at boot. backend/ai-coach/run.sh is the entrypoint the Lambda
# Web Adapter runs, and scripts/*.sh run in CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
